This PR fix match expr with non last if expr  (fix #9419).

- Fix match expr with non last if expr.
- Add test.

```v
fn main() {
	out := match true {
		true {
			{
			}
			if true {
			} else {
			}
			'a'
		}
		else {
			for {
				break
			}
			'b'
		}
	}
	println(out)
	assert out == 'a'
}

PS D:\Test\v\tt1> v run .
a
```
if non-last expr is not C expression, it will check error like this:
```v
fn main() {
	out := match true {
		true {
			404
			'a'
		}
		else {
			'b'
		}
	}
	println(out)
	assert out == 'a'
}

PS D:\Test\v\tt1> v run .
./tt1.v:4:4: error: expression evaluated but not used
    2 |     out := match true {
    3 |         true {
    4 |             404
      |             ~~~
    5 |             'a'
    6 |         }
```

